; SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
;
; varek_container: the one SELinux rule VAREK's container needs (v1.32, D5
; in docs/security/v1.32-containers.md), for Podman (or Docker) on RHEL,
; Fedora and others with SELinux enforcing.
;
; The container runs as container_init_t, the distribution's own type for
; containers that manage their control groups (Podman uses it for systemd
; in a container): container_t, with cgroup_t directories and files
; managed, as sub-agents and confined MCP servers need (v1.28.1, v1.31).
; The runtime mounts the container's cgroup filesystem read-only, and the
; Warden remounts it read-write (its own groups only: --cgroupns=private);
; container_init_t may not remount it, which is the first rule below; nor
; mount on a character device (the noexec mount of /dev/null, which a policy
; letting the agent write it has the Warden bind onto itself: v1.27.1), the
; second. Both measured on RHEL 9.8. Other
; containers keep container_t; this is not the host-wide
; container_manage_cgroup boolean.
;
; On the host, as root:
;
;   semodule -i varek_container.cil
;
; and run the container with --security-opt label=type:container_init_t,
; with the settings in packaging/container/README.md.

(allow container_init_t cgroup_t (filesystem (remount)))
(allow container_init_t container_file_t (chr_file (mounton)))
